    "first_run_reason": "Vulkan is 33.5 MB and covers every desktop GPU vendor, so it is the cheapest fetch that turns on offload. NVIDIA is mapped to Vulkan too, which is a change from the earlier assumption that CUDA was worth 537 MB on NVIDIA hardware: see `measured`. CUDA remains pinned and installable on request through HEARTH_GPU_ENGINE.",
    "measured": {
      "conclusion": "CUDA and Vulkan trade wins within a few per cent of each other on this card: CUDA is 5 to 7 per cent faster at prompt processing on the 7B, Vulkan is 25 per cent faster at prompt processing on the 0.5B F16, and token generation is identical to three significant figures on the 7B. Either is roughly twelve times the CPU build at generation and forty-five times at prompt processing. A margin that small does not justify 504 MB of extra download, so NVIDIA gets Vulkan like everybody else.",
